{
  "dom_id": "step-q85325",
  "name": "Question 10",
  "problem": "A programmer reviews his web page and notices that, on average, $7$ visitors view his page every minute. What is the probability that there will be $5$ visitors in the next minute? Round your answer to $3$ decimal places. You may assume that visitors connect to the site independently and at a constant average rate.",
  "worked_solution": "A Poisson random variable $X$ with rate $\\lambda $ has the following probability mass function:\n\n$$\nf(x)=\\frac{{\\lambda }^{x}{e}^{-\\lambda }}{x!}\n$$\n\nLet $X$ be the number of visitors to the web page. Since the average rate is $7$ visitors per minute, and events occur independently and at a constant average rate, the number of visitors can be modeled as a Poisson random variable with rate $\\lambda =7,$ and we can write $X∼\\text{Po}(7).$ \n\nSo, $X$ has the following probability mass function:\n\n$$\nf(x)=\\frac{{7}^{x}{e}^{-7}}{x!}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the probability of having $5$ visitors in the next minute is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(X=5) & =f(5) \\\\  & =\\frac{{7}^{5}{e}^{-7}}{5!} \\\\  & ≈0.128\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nrounded to $3$ decimal places.",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
